# Multi-machine cellGPU

This repo is cloned on several SSH hosts (clusters and workstations). GitHub `master` is the source of truth for shared simulation code. Each host has its own CUDA/compiler modules and job scripts. Do not copy `src/` between machines by hand.

## Shared (edit and commit)

- `src/`, `inc/`
- Simulation drivers (`glassyDynamicsProject/*.cpp`, `agingProject/`, `MCTProject/`, `gdRelaxation/`, `examples/`)
- Portable analysis scripts (`.wl`/`.wls`, Python)
- Mathematica `*.nb`: commit from the analysis clone to origin only; simulation clones sparse-checkout them out (see `mathematica-notebooks.mdc`)
- Reusable submit *templates* with no host paths, partitions, or accounts

## Local only (never commit)

- Root `CMakeLists.txt` (already gitignored; per-host include/lib/CUDA paths)
- `local/` — this host's `env.sh`, module loads, and submit scripts
- `data/`, binaries (`*.out`, `*.o`), and `build/` artifacts
- Absolute paths such as `/home/chengling/...` or `/u/...`

Put new host-specific submit scripts in `local/submit/`. Existing files under `*/localSubmissionScript/` may already contain host paths; do not rewrite them for another machine unless asked.

## Agent behavior

- After changing shared source, other hosts need `git pull` then a rebuild before new jobs.
- Do not `git add .`. Stage only shared source.
- Do not rebuild over a binary a running job is using; use a new `build-*` dir instead.
- Do not leave `cursor-agent` workers or other daemons on cluster login nodes (see `delta-login-nodes.mdc`).
- Prefer relative paths or `$CELLGPU_ROOT` in any script that is committed.
- Record `git rev-parse HEAD` in new submit scripts so runs are reproducible.
